<tt xmlns="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml" xmlns:itunes="http://music.apple.com/lyric-ttml-internal" xmlns:ttm="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml#metadata" itunes:timing="Line" xml:lang="en"><head><metadata><ttm:agent type="person" xml:id="v1"/><ttm:agent type="person" xml:id="v2"/><iTunesMetadata xmlns="http://music.apple.com/lyric-ttml-internal" leadingSilence="0"><translations/><songwriters><songwriter>A. Brown</songwriter><songwriter>Dido</songwriter><songwriter>K. Brown</songwriter><songwriter>Patrick Held</songwriter><songwriter>Paul Herman</songwriter></songwriters></iTunesMetadata></metadata></head><body dur="3:18.904"><div begin="27.183" end="53.376" itunes:songPart="Chorus"><p begin="27.183" end="33.433" itunes:key="L1" ttm:agent="v1">My lean's gone cold, I'm wondering why I got out bed at all</p><p begin="33.920" end="40.190" itunes:key="L2" ttm:agent="v1">3.5 clouds up my window, and I can't see at all</p><p begin="40.368" end="46.742" itunes:key="L3" ttm:agent="v1">And even if I could, it would all be grey, but these racks stacked up too tall</p><p begin="47.086" end="53.376" itunes:key="L4" ttm:agent="v1">It reminds me that it's not so bad, it's not so bad at all</p></div><div begin="53.023" end="1:32.181" itunes:songPart="Verse"><p begin="53.023" end="56.181" itunes:key="L5" ttm:agent="v1">Fuck sitting on the windows, been playing with the bands like Dido (Dido)</p><p begin="56.191" end="59.046" itunes:key="L6" ttm:agent="v1">Outdoor smoking endo by my lonely, like a widow</p><p begin="59.400" end="1:02.341" itunes:key="L7" ttm:agent="v1">Ice cubes, pour me some more, she pop like a pistol</p><p begin="1:02.733" end="1:05.760" itunes:key="L8" ttm:agent="v1">Push start new vehicle, I done jumped out, G.I. Joe</p><p begin="1:06.014" end="1:09.077" itunes:key="L9" ttm:agent="v1">God forgives but I don't, Lord have mercy, I don't</p><p begin="1:09.662" end="1:12.567" itunes:key="L10" ttm:agent="v1">Big shot, big dog, block too hot, gotta cool off (Cool off)</p><p begin="1:12.567" end="1:15.889" itunes:key="L11" ttm:agent="v1">CCTV running 24/7, you better not move wrong (Move wrong)</p><p begin="1:15.889" end="1:19.188" itunes:key="L12" ttm:agent="v1">I can see the wallet chain hanging out my shadows (Shadows)</p><p begin="1:19.188" end="1:22.241" itunes:key="L13" ttm:agent="v1">USDs and Euros, I do 'em so foul, two free throws</p><p begin="1:22.621" end="1:25.508" itunes:key="L14" ttm:agent="v1">Just left the jeweler, weigh my neck down with two kilos</p><p begin="1:25.725" end="1:28.857" itunes:key="L15" ttm:agent="v1">It's you, it's not me though, speed limit sixty over</p><p begin="1:29.039" end="1:32.181" itunes:key="L16" ttm:agent="v1">Twist up 3.5 and I smell older, I'm in the ozone</p></div><div begin="1:32.933" end="1:59.089" itunes:songPart="Chorus"><p begin="1:32.933" end="1:39.349" itunes:key="L17" ttm:agent="v1">My lean's gone cold, I'm wondering why I got out bed at all</p><p begin="1:39.704" end="1:45.899" itunes:key="L18" ttm:agent="v1">3.5 clouds up my window, and I can't see at all</p><p begin="1:46.121" end="1:52.483" itunes:key="L19" ttm:agent="v1">And even if I could, it would all be grey, but these racks stacked up too tall</p><p begin="1:52.854" end="1:59.089" itunes:key="L20" ttm:agent="v1">It reminds me that it's not so bad, it's not so bad at all</p></div><div begin="1:58.815" end="2:38.490" itunes:songPart="Verse" ttm:agent="v2"><p begin="1:58.815" end="2:02.128" itunes:key="L21" ttm:agent="v2">Started off in last place, started passing ****</p><p begin="2:02.128" end="2:05.190" itunes:key="L22" ttm:agent="v2">I always had faith, never saw no competition</p><p begin="2:05.367" end="2:11.215" itunes:key="L23" ttm:agent="v2">Never saw no competition, lately I don't know why I been reminiscing, hey</p><p begin="2:11.755" end="2:14.882" itunes:key="L24" ttm:agent="v2">More money, more problems, but I think I like those problems</p><p begin="2:14.882" end="2:17.965" itunes:key="L25" ttm:agent="v2">They see me winning now, but you ain't see me when I was starving</p><p begin="2:18.144" end="2:21.231" itunes:key="L26" ttm:agent="v2">You ain't know me at the bottom, you wasn't with me on that grind</p><p begin="2:21.427" end="2:25.424" itunes:key="L27" ttm:agent="v2">Couldn't call you when I was a hurting, so I ain't gon' call you when I shine (Yeah, yeah)</p><p begin="2:25.522" end="2:31.173" itunes:key="L28" ttm:agent="v2">The lean's gone cold, the lean's gone cold 'cause I don't pour up any more</p><p begin="2:31.506" end="2:38.490" itunes:key="L29" ttm:agent="v2">Eyes so low that I can't roll up anymore, but I'm a lonely stoner so I'm still gon' smoke one more, yeah, yeah</p></div><div begin="2:38.679" end="3:05.115" itunes:songPart="Chorus"><p begin="2:38.679" end="2:45.125" itunes:key="L30" ttm:agent="v1">My lean's gone cold, I'm wondering why I got out of bed at all</p><p begin="2:45.422" end="2:51.894" itunes:key="L31" ttm:agent="v1">3.5 clouds up my window, and I can't see at all (Yeah)</p><p begin="2:51.894" end="2:58.299" itunes:key="L32" ttm:agent="v1">And even if I could, it would all be grey, but these racks stacked up too tall</p><p begin="2:58.603" end="3:05.115" itunes:key="L33" ttm:agent="v1">It reminds me, that it's not so bad, it's not so bad at all</p></div></body></tt>